From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcus Ramberg <marcus@means.no>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:53:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] media: i2c: imx858: fix power-on reset/clock ordering

imx858_power_on() released the sensor reset (XCLR) before enabling the
input clock and only waited ~1ms afterwards. Sony sensors require the
reset to be deasserted only after MCLK is running and stable. The cold
boot path happened to work due to incidental settle time, but a
runtime-PM power-down/up cycle (e.g. restarting the camera app) races:
the sensor does not re-initialise, the first i2c access NAKs, and the
GENI i2c controller wedges ("Timeout resetting RX_FSM"), taking the AF
actuator on the same bus down with it.

Reorder to match the working s5kjn1 driver: enable regulators, enable
MCLK, let it settle, then release reset and wait for the sensor to boot
before the first i2c transaction.

Signed-off-by: Marcus Ramberg <marcus@means.no>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx858.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx858.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx858.c
index 4f261e70ea6f..121a0d747f77 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx858.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx858.c
@@ -1073,20 +1073,23 @@ static int imx858_power_on(struct device *dev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(imx858->reset_gpio, 0);
-
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(imx858->inclk);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(imx858->dev, "fail to enable inclk\n");
-		goto error_reset;
+		goto error_regulator;
 	}
 
+	/* Let the input clock (MCLK) settle before releasing reset (XCLR). */
 	usleep_range(1000, 1200);
 
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(imx858->reset_gpio, 0);
+
+	/* Wait for the sensor to boot before the first i2c access. */
+	usleep_range(10000, 15000);
+
 	return 0;
 
-error_reset:
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(imx858->reset_gpio, 1);
+error_regulator:
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(imx858_supply_names),
 			       imx858->supplies);
 
